<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador monetary base down 2.37 pct in Jan 17 week.</title>
<headline>Ecuador monetary base down 2.37 pct in Jan 17 week.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's monetary base fell 2.37 percent to 2.84 billion sucres in the week to January 17, the Central Bank said Monday.</p>
<p>In December 1996, money base grew 12.4 percent to 3.03 billion sucres.</p>
<p>The bank gave no reason for the fall.</p>
<p>The monetary base ended 1996 at 3.06 billion sucres, up from 2.41 billion sucres at the end of 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
</text>
